          answer: 'Any even number can be written as 2n, where n is an integer, so two consecutive even numbers are 2n and 2n + 2. Their product is 2n(2n + 2) = 4n(n + 1). Now n and n + 1 are consecutive integers, so exactly one of them is even, which means n(n + 1) is always even and can be written as 2k. The product is therefore 4 × 2k = 8k, a multiple of 8. Since n was any integer, this holds for every such pair.',
